msgid "Coexistence"
msgstr ""

#: luci-app-uugamebooster/luasrc/model/cbi/uuplugin.lua:88
msgid "Split the traffic (recommended)"
msgstr ""

#: luci-app-uugamebooster/luasrc/model/cbi/uuplugin.lua:89
msgid "Take whole devices off OpenClash"
msgstr ""

#: luci-app-uugamebooster/luasrc/model/cbi/uuplugin.lua:90
msgid "Leave OpenClash alone"
msgstr ""

#: luci-app-uugamebooster/luasrc/model/cbi/uuplugin.lua:92
msgid "UU and OpenClash both intercept LAN traffic, so left alone one of them silently wins.<br /><br /><strong>Split the traffic</strong> lets each handle what it is for. Only what UU actually accelerates leaves OpenClash: the game servers UU routes into its tunnel, plus the UDP ports it marks - both read back from UU's own live rules, for boosted devices only. Everything else from that same device keeps going through OpenClash.<br /><em>So most of a boosted PC's traffic still going through OpenClash is the intended result, not a fault.</em><br /><br /><strong>Take whole devices off OpenClash</strong> is the blunt fallback: the devices you list stop using the proxy entirely while UU runs.<br /><strong>Leave OpenClash alone</strong> changes nothing - useful if you would rather tune OpenClash by hand."
msgstr ""

#: luci-app-uugamebooster/luasrc/model/cbi/uuplugin.lua:108
msgid "Move devices off OpenClash's own bypass list"
msgstr ""

#: luci-app-uugamebooster/luasrc/model/cbi/uuplugin.lua:109
msgid "OpenClash keeps a list of devices that skip the proxy completely (lan_ac_black_ips). A boosted device on that list skips OpenClash for everything, so the split above can do nothing for it. Turn this on to let the plugin take such a device off OpenClash's list while it is boosted and put it back afterwards. Off by default, because it edits and saves OpenClash's configuration."
msgstr ""

#: luci-app-uugamebooster/luasrc/model/cbi/uuplugin.lua:119
msgid "Devices to bypass - by MAC"
msgstr ""

#: luci-app-uugamebooster/luasrc/model/cbi/uuplugin.lua:120
msgid "These stop using OpenClash while UU is running."
msgstr ""

#: luci-app-uugamebooster/luasrc/model/cbi/uuplugin.lua:125
msgid "Devices to bypass - by IP"
msgstr ""

#: luci-app-uugamebooster/luasrc/model/cbi/uuplugin.lua:126
msgid "Addresses or CIDR ranges that stop using OpenClash while UU runs."
msgstr ""

#: luci-app-uugamebooster/luasrc/model/cbi/uuplugin.lua:131
msgid "How often to re-check UU's routes"
msgstr ""

#: luci-app-uugamebooster/luasrc/model/cbi/uuplugin.lua:132
msgid "In seconds. UU adds and removes game routes as it goes."
msgstr ""

#: luci-app-uugamebooster/luasrc/model/cbi/uuplugin.lua:138
msgid "Widest route to divert"
msgstr ""

#: luci-app-uugamebooster/luasrc/model/cbi/uuplugin.lua:139
msgid "A safety limit, as a prefix length: never send a route broader than this around OpenClash. Stops one stray default route from pulling the whole internet out of the proxy."
msgstr ""

#: luci-app-uugamebooster/luasrc/model/cbi/uuplugin.lua:149
msgid "Keep PassWall's DNS (recommended)"
msgstr ""

#: luci-app-uugamebooster/luasrc/model/cbi/uuplugin.lua:150
msgid "Leave PassWall alone"
msgstr ""

#: luci-app-uugamebooster/luasrc/model/cbi/uuplugin.lua:154
msgid "How often to re-check UU's DNS redirect"
msgstr ""

#: luci-app-uugamebooster/luasrc/model/cbi/uuplugin.lua:155
msgid "In seconds. UU re-inserts its redirect at the top of the chain every time a boost starts, so this decides how quickly it gets pushed back."
msgstr ""

#: luci-app-uugamebooster/luasrc/model/cbi/uuplugin.lua:164
msgid "PassWall splits traffic at the routing layer and UU at its own policy rule, so a boosted device's game traffic already goes into UU's tunnel and everything else into the proxy."
msgstr ""

#: luci-app-uugamebooster/luasrc/model/cbi/uuplugin.lua:166
msgid "What collides is DNS: UU sends each boosted device's UDP/53 into the game tunnel and blocks its IPv6 DNS outright, which bypasses PassWall's resolver chain. UU never removes the IPv6 block, so that device cannot resolve over IPv6 until the next reboot."
msgstr ""

#: luci-app-uugamebooster/luasrc/model/cbi/uuplugin.lua:168
msgid "<strong>Keep PassWall's DNS</strong> puts the router's own address back in front of that redirect and removes the IPv6 block. UU only checks that its rule was accepted, not that packets reach it, so acceleration is unaffected."
msgstr ""

#: luci-app-uugamebooster/luasrc/model/cbi/uuplugin.lua:170
msgid "<strong>Leave PassWall alone</strong> changes nothing."
msgstr ""

#: luci-app-uugamebooster/luasrc/model/cbi/uuplugin.lua:172
msgid "Nothing happens unless PassWall is installed."
msgstr ""

#: luci-app-uugamebooster/luasrc/model/cbi/uuplugin.lua:177
msgid "Keep game traffic out of UA3F (recommended)"
msgstr ""

#: luci-app-uugamebooster/luasrc/model/cbi/uuplugin.lua:178
msgid "Leave UA3F alone"
msgstr ""

#: luci-app-uugamebooster/luasrc/model/cbi/uuplugin.lua:180
msgid "UA3F rewrites the User-Agent of LAN traffic by diverting TCP to itself, which also takes a boosted device's game connections away from UU.<br /><br /><strong>Keep game traffic out of UA3F</strong> exempts only the game servers UU routes into its tunnel, and only for boosted devices. Everything else from that device, its web browsing included, still goes through UA3F.<br /><strong>Leave UA3F alone</strong> changes nothing.<br />Nothing happens unless UA3F is installed and running."
msgstr ""

#: luci-app-uugamebooster/luasrc/model/cbi/uuplugin.lua:193
msgid "Keep game traffic out of HomeProxy (recommended)"
msgstr ""

#: luci-app-uugamebooster/luasrc/model/cbi/uuplugin.lua:194
msgid "Leave HomeProxy alone"
msgstr ""

#: luci-app-uugamebooster/luasrc/model/cbi/uuplugin.lua:196
msgid "With its TUN inbound and auto-redirect, HomeProxy redirects LAN TCP to sing-box before UU can route it, so a boosted device's game connections fail while its UDP still works.<br /><br /><strong>Keep game traffic out of HomeProxy</strong> exempts the game servers UU routes into its tunnel, and the device's DNS, only for boosted devices. Everything else from that device still goes through HomeProxy.<br /><strong>Leave HomeProxy alone</strong> changes nothing.<br /><br />HomeProxy's other modes are not handled. There, add the device under HomeProxy's Access Control, with <em>Proxy all except listed</em>; it then skips HomeProxy entirely.<br />The polling interval and widest route come from the OpenClash tab."
msgstr ""

#: luci-app-uugamebooster/luasrc/model/cbi/uuplugin.lua:213
msgid "Devices UU is allowed to see"
msgstr ""

#: luci-app-uugamebooster/luasrc/model/cbi/uuplugin.lua:214
msgid "Every device on the network"
msgstr ""

#: luci-app-uugamebooster/luasrc/model/cbi/uuplugin.lua:215
msgid "Everything except the devices below"
msgstr ""

#: luci-app-uugamebooster/luasrc/model/cbi/uuplugin.lua:216
msgid "Only the devices below"
msgstr ""

#: luci-app-uugamebooster/luasrc/model/cbi/uuplugin.lua:218
msgid "The UU app lists whatever the plugin finds on your network, which by default is everything. This narrows what it can find at all, so a device left out never appears in the app, is never offered for boosting, and is never reported to NetEase.<br />Nothing else on the router is affected: the real DHCP leases and ARP table are untouched, and no traffic is blocked."
msgstr ""

